Z||000001||2xsess||12-21-2000||02:51 PM||||If it's an aluminum or alloy wheel you should take it some where because you can break the wheel. <P>Plus it's a real pain if you don't have the right equipment.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||12-21-2000||05:55 PM||||i did it a few times a long time ago but they were steel wheels and cars had a different type of jack. i used the old style jack that hooked to the bumper and kind of put the base of the jack right at the edge of the wheel. then when you jack up the car the base presses down and breaks the bead (did that make sence?). then you take it off like you would a bicycle tire. more trouble than it's worth unless you're really desperate.||||reg||1
